5 #edb/ref 17592186523728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523886 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523886 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523886 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186523406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523886 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c10c01cc-e0f9-571f-a0fb-7e4e517f6d40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523894 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523894 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523894 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523894 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523894 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523894 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523894 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523894 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186523626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523894 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d79f42f3-7a3e-5cfc-ae54-7f17a62555f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523925 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523925 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95894" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523925 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523925 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x}{2x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523925 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04ba3fd8-1522-5fe9-a412-8ecb77ad06a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523925 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x$ and $v(x)=2x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x)}^{′}\\cdot 2x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x\\cdot {(2x)}^{′}}{{(2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2{csch}^{2}⁡2x)\\cdot 2x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x\\cdot (2)}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2(2x{csch}^{2}⁡2x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x)}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x{csch}^{2}⁡2x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x}{2{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523940 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523940 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95587" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523940 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523940 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=x{sech}^{2}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523940 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "26dd88c1-a8ad-595c-af19-c13d906feda9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523940 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)={sech}^{2}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(x)}^{′}\\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡x+x\\cdot {({sech}^{2}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =1\\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡x+x\\cdot (2\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x) \\\\  & ={sech}^{2}⁡x-2x{sech}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x \\\\  & ={sech}^{2}⁡x(1-2x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523987 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523987 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95575" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523987 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523987 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=3{csch}^{2}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523987 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9541bdac-540f-537e-a50e-b6a223ada95f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523987 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=3{g}^{2},\\,g=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=6g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =6g(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-6{csch}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524008 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524008 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95567" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524008 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524008 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=-2\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524008 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c4169769-2e08-50ac-8627-9cd65f653a9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524008 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=-2\\operatorname{coth}⁡g,\\,g=4x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=2{csch}^{2}\\,g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2{csch}^{2}⁡g\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8{csch}^{2}⁡g \\\\  & =8{csch}^{2}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524065 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186524098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524065 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "67b9f987-8c65-5ef3-b902-335deeb911ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524065 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186523940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524087 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186524101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524087 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ad7abaa3-35f9-55c7-b149-f9e8e8e19cba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524087 #edb/